      "title": "I Believe She's Giving Up on Me",
      "slug": "wwyd-ibelivesheisgivingup",
      "category_slug": "what-will-you-do",
      "excerpt": "My relationship with my mother, someone I have always looked up to and relied on, \nis falling apart, and I feel like she is giving up on me. I need help understanding\nwhat went wrong and how to fix it.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "My relationship with my mother, someone I have always looked up to and relied on, \nis falling apart, and I feel like she is giving up on me. I need help understanding\nwhat went wrong and how to fix it.",
        "Growing up, my mother, Linda, was my rock. She was always there for me, supporting me\nthrough every challenge and celebrating every success. We were incredibly close, and \nI always felt that our bond was unbreakable. However, over the past year, things have\nchanged dramatically, and I am struggling to understand why.",
        "I am in my mid-twenties, and like many people my age, I have faced my share of difficulties. \nAfter graduating from college, I struggled to find a stable job in my field. I took on various\npart-time jobs to make ends meet, but nothing seemed to stick. My mother was initially supportive, \nencouraging me to keep trying and reassuring me that I would eventually find my path.",
        "However, as the months went by and I continued to struggle, I noticed a change in her attitude. \nShe became more distant and critical, often making remarks about my inability to get my life together.\nEvery conversation seemed to turn into a lecture about my perceived failures, and I felt like I could \nnever do anything right in her eyes.",
        "I lost another job a few weeks ago, and that was the tipping point. I contacted my mother for assistance, \nfeeling dejected and desperate. Instead of the reassuring words I expected, she showed dissatisfaction \nand frustration. She told me she was weary of picking up the pieces all the time and that it was time \nfor me to mature and accept responsibility for my own life.",
        "Her words cut deeply, and I felt a profound sense of abandonment. The person who had always been my biggest \ncheerleader was now making me feel like a burden. Since that conversation, our interactions have become even \nmore strained. She rarely calls or visits, and when we do talk, it feels like she's just going through the \nmotions.",
        "Adding to the tension, I recently had a run-in with the law. It was a minor incident—a misunderstanding that \nled to a night in jail. I was released without charges, but the experience was humiliating, and I had to \ncall my mother to bail me out. Instead of sympathy, I was met with anger and disappointment. She told \nme she was ashamed of me and couldn't believe I had put myself in such a situation.",
        "Financially, things haven't been great either. I've had to borrow money from my mother several times \nto cover rent and bills. While she initially helped without hesitation, lately she's been expressing \nfrustration about my lack of financial independence. She has hinted that she's tired of being my \nsafety net and that I need to learn to stand on my own two feet.",
        "On top of everything, I've also been struggling with my mental health. Anxiety and depression have \nmade it hard for me to stay motivated and focused. I've tried to explain this to my mother, hoping \nfor understanding and support, but she seems to see it as just another excuse. She tells me I need \nto be stronger and stop letting life beat me down.",
        "I have had thoughts of ending it all, I am at a loss. I love my mother dearly, and don’t know how \nto repair our relationship, and I don't know how to bridge the growing gap between us. I feel like \nshe has given up on me, and I am left feeling alone and unsupported during one of the most challenging \ntimes of my life.",
        "I am seeking advice from anyone who has been in a similar situation or who can offer guidance on how \nto navigate this painful and complex dilemma. How do I rebuild my relationship with my mother and\nregain her support and trust? Is it possible to mend the rift that has developed between us, or \nhave we reached a point of no return? How can I find the strength to keep going when I feel like \nthe one person I need the most has given up on me?"
      ],
